# shir_nodes/clone_deep.node — CloneDeep: a DEEP COPY of any store value
# (`x.clone()` under the Rust Clone bound).
#
# GENERIC. Soundness: Rust's clone NEVER aliases the original (that is
# the contract of the Clone bound), so an independent deep copy is the
# exact semantics for every store-representable value (strings, numbers,
# arrays, records). An IDENTITY lowering would be the aliasing bug the
# value-store model must not guess.
# Backends: JS structuredClone(value) (Node >=17 global); other backends
# may refuse until they pick their deep-copy primitive (Perl would be
# Storable::dclone).

node CloneDeep
tag "CloneDeep"
kind expr
field value: expr
